title: Widgets
---

<script>
  import Demo from "$lib/docs/Demo.svelte";
</script>

A widget is a home-screen card. It's a pure function that returns a
**description** of what to show — the app renders it from a fixed set of
[primitives](/docs/plugins/primitives). No markup, no components.

## The contract

```ts
export const pluginBundle = {
  formatVersion: 1,
  pluginId: "com.you.week-recap",
  family: "widget",
  entryExport: "widget",
} as const;

export const widget = {
  id: "com.you.week-recap",
  name: "Week Recap",
  description: "Sessions, sets and volume in the last 7 days.",
  needs: ["workouts"],

  compute(input) {
    const since = input.now - 7 * 864e5;
    let sessions = 0, sets = 0, tonnage = 0;
    for (const w of input.workouts ?? []) {
      if (!w.endedAtMs || w.endedAtMs < since) continue;
      sessions++;
      for (const ex of w.exercises)
        for (const s of ex.sets) { sets++; tonnage += s.weight * s.reps; }
    }

    if (sessions === 0) {
      return {
        title: "Week Recap",
        body: [],
        empty: { text: "Nothing logged in the last 7 days.", action: { startEmptyWorkout: true } },
      };
    }

    return {
      title: "Week Recap",
      subtitle: "Last 7 days",
      body: [{
        kind: "stat-grid",
        stats: [
          { label: "Sessions", value: String(sessions) },
          { label: "Sets", value: String(sets) },
          { label: "Volume", value: Math.round(tonnage).toLocaleString() + " kg" },
        ],
      }],
      action: { navigate: "/sessions" },
    };
  },
};
```

<Demo title="What that renders" node={{ kind: "stat-grid", stats: [
  { label: "Sessions", value: "3" },
  { label: "Sets", value: "42" },
  { label: "Volume", value: "18,400 kg" },
]}} />

## Declaring `needs`

The host only loads the data slices you ask for, and only serialises those into
the sandbox. Ask for the minimum.

| Need | You get |
|---|---|
| `workouts` | recent sessions (capped ~200 days / 150), each with exercises + sets |
| `exercises` | the exercise catalogue with muscle groups |
| `session` | `{ active, hasPlan, plannedDayLabel? }` |
| `todaysPlan` | `{ splitId?, dayLabel?, scheduled, dayIndex?, dayCount?, exercises: string[] }` |
| `progressionTargets` | `{ exerciseName, target }[]` — the host runs the algorithm |
| `nutrition` | `{ hasGoal, targetKcal?, consumedKcal?, targetMacros?, consumedMacros? }` |
| `bodyweight` | `{ currentKg?, weeklyRateKg?, targetKg?, trendPoints }` |

Full input type: `@logit/core/plugins/widgetView` → `WidgetInput`.

## The view

```ts
type WidgetView = {
  title: string;
  subtitle?: string;
  body: WidgetNode[];             // stacked primitives
  action?: WidgetAction;          // tap the card
  headerActions?: { icon: "add" | "edit" | "prev" | "next"; label; action }[];
  pager?: { count: number; index: number };
  swipe?: { left: WidgetAction; right: WidgetAction };
  empty?: { text: string; action?: WidgetAction };  // shown instead of body
};
```

## Actions

Widgets can't navigate freely or run code. `WidgetAction` is an allow-list:

- `{ navigate: "/some/app/path" }` — internal routes only
- `{ startEmptyWorkout: true }` · `{ startPlannedWorkout: true }` · `{ resumeWorkout: true }`
- `{ cycleDay: -1 | 1 }` — move the previewed split day

See the [primitive gallery](/docs/plugins/primitives) for every node type with
live examples.
